l="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-8222252-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>8222252</doc-number> <kind>A</kind> </document-id> <sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1176219A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURIIWA TAKAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOHOKU TECHNO ARCH CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURIIWA, TAKAHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOHOKU TECHNO ARCH CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURIIWA TAKAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKADA MASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURIIWA, TAKAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKADA, MASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for absorbing and releasing which comprises repeating the application of a hydrogen pressure to an alloy for hydrogen storage having a body-centered cubic structure and exhibiting two step or gradient plateau property in the relationship between the amount of the hydrogen absorbed and the pressure of hydrogen and the exposure of the alloy under reduced pressure, characterized in that, at least for a period of time in the process of hydrogen release, the temperature of the alloy in the process of hydrogen release (T2) is lower than that in the process of hydrogen absorption, that is T2 &gt; T1. The method allows the release and use of the hydrogen stored in the lower pressure region in a two step plateau or the lower portion region of a gradient plateau.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé d'absorption et de libération consistant à appliquer à plusieurs reprises une pression d'hydrogène sur un alliage de stockage d'hydrogène présentant une structure cubique à corps central et doté d'une propriété de plateau à gradient ou étage double en termes de rapport entre la quantité d'hydrogène absorbée et de la pression d'hydrogène et l'exposition de l'alliage à une pression réduite. Au cours de la libération d'hydrogène (T2) et pendant un certain laps de temps au moins, la température de l'alliage est inférieure à celle à laquelle se produit l'absorption d'hydrogène, T2 est donc supérieur à T1. Ce procédé permet la libération et l'utilisation de l'hydrogène stocké dans la zone de pression inférieure dans un plateau à étage double ou dans la zone de la partie inférieure d'un plateau à gradient.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms 